  "rule_description": "JEP 400 changed Charset.defaultCharset() to return UTF-8 from JDK 18, and with it every java.io constructor that encodes or decodes without an explicit charset. The JEP names them: InputStreamReader, FileReader, OutputStreamWriter, FileWriter and PrintStream. Nothing breaks and nothing warns -- the code compiles identically on 17 and 21 -- but a file written by a JDK 17 JVM on a windows-1252 host and read by a JDK 21 JVM is silently corrupted, which is the exact hazard the JEP describes. This rule covers only the sites where JADE writes a file it later reads back itself: persisted messages, fault recovery state, log and CSV output. Sites whose stream comes from a socket carry the same question as the ACL and JICP wire codecs and are deliberately excluded; that is a protocol compatibility decision for the maintainer.",
  "rule_id": "JEP400_FILE_IO_DEFAULT_CHARSET",
  "rule_name": "File readers, writers and print streams without an explicit charset switched from the platform default to UTF-8 in JDK 18",
